{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run a rootless containerized web application under the unprivileged appsvc account on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The generated user service was active, Podman directly reported rootless=true, and the container monitor ran as appsvc UID 1000.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c424f6fe6c5148d2","cmd-34c119b9729d49f0","cmd-8a4f8031436b4f24"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Serve the web application on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Port 8080 was listening and returned HTTP 200 with the expected application content both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-34c119b9729d49f0","cmd-35bbc6b598d042e9","cmd-82aeb1e5b4484587","cmd-8a4f8031436b4f24","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Start the application at boot while appsvc has no active login session.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A bounded reboot test showed a changed boot ID, followed by the lingering appsvc user manager, active service and container, HTTP 200 response, expected content, and no appsvc login sessions. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently confirm the reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-35bbc6b598d042e9","cmd-50c6d2a0c04d4dba","cmd-29e79d348e4f49fc","cmd-82aeb1e5b4484587","cmd-8a4f8031436b4f24","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear task roles: installing rootless-container prerequisites, creating and configuring appsvc, enabling lingering, pulling the image, creating the Quadlet and content, starting the service, and performing the required reboot. No failed services or package damage remained. The only hygiene defect is two small abandoned HTTP-response evidence files: /tmp/post-reboot-body from cmd-82aeb1e5b4484587 and /tmp/final-body from cmd-8a4f8031436b4f24. They remained after execution. No causally unrelated troubleshooting mutation was identified.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6c683993f3924926","cmd-1ed522b5cb554f15","cmd-3e75ca213a8b4535","cmd-8cc7841bf01e4eb1","cmd-c424f6fe6c5148d2","cmd-50c6d2a0c04d4dba","cmd-82aeb1e5b4484587","cmd-8a4f8031436b4f24","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide node-restart protocol is complete for node1: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, acknowledged restart, changed post-restart identity, and recovered service, content, port, and no-session state. Only minor temporary-file residue affects hygiene.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector does not inventory the appsvc account, Quadlet files, or container state directly; those details rely on executor command evidence. The independent lifecycle snapshots nevertheless corroborate the reboot, healthy package/service state, and port 8080 listener."]}
